 "legal": "The commission makes findings; Preamble relays what trusted news outlets report from its public hearings, word for word and credited. Being named in evidence is not a finding of wrongdoing, and a charge is not a conviction.",
 "explainer": [
  "In July 2025, KwaZulu-Natal police commissioner Lt Gen Nhlanhla Mkhwanazi publicly alleged that criminal networks had infiltrated the police and justice system, and that senior officials interfered in investigations. President Cyril Ramaphosa set up a judicial commission of inquiry, chaired by retired Constitutional Court Justice Mbuyiseli Madlanga, to investigate.",
  "The commission hears evidence in public, and some of it behind closed doors. It will make findings and recommendations to the President; it cannot convict anyone."
 ],
 "timeline": [
  [
   "July 2025",
   "Mkhwanazi’s briefing alleging political interference in policing"
  ],
